            "title": "JitRL -- 无参数后训练",
            "date_published": "2026-11-03T16:00:00.000Z",
            "content_html": "<link rel=\"stylesheet\" type=\"text/css\" href=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/hint.css/2.4.1/hint.min.css\"><h1 id=\"jitrl\"><a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#jitrl\">#</a> JitRL</h1>\n<p>常见的模型后训练都发生在模型权重上，对于全参数模型的后训练的资源开销巨大，小模型本地推理在能力和计算资源开销上较大。</p>\n<p>在Agentic 时代，API调用下只能通过设备端的Prompt优化，但只有Prompt 并不能稳定持续优化特定领域任务。</p>\n<p>与Train-free RL 相关的工作不同，JitRL在设备端实现一个简单KNN回归，保留了RL中基本的Advantage estimation和 Optimation, 但并不基于模型的本身token分布Rollout策略</p>\n<p><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><munder><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">arg max</mi><mo>⁡</mo></mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo mathvariant=\"normal\" lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">′</mo></msup></munder><mrow><mo fence=\"true\">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">E</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo mathvariant=\"normal\" lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo mathvariant=\"normal\" lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">′</mo></msup><mo>∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mi>l</mi><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo fence=\"true\">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\pi^\\ast = \\argmax_{\\pi&#x27;} \\left(\\mathbb E_{a\\sim \\pi&#x27;}[A(s,a)]-\\beta D_{KL}(\\pi&#x27;\\parallel \\pi_{old})\\right)\n</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.7387em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.03588em;\">π</span><span 